Run.Description Twisted bilayer graphene (6.009 degrees): spectral function unfolded on the graphene lattice
Run.Prefix generate
Run.TypeOfSystem TwistedBilayerBasedOnMoireCell
Structure.MoireCellParameters 6 5 5 6
Structure.SuperCell 1
Stack.TwoLayers .true.
Stack.TwoLayersZ1 18.325
Stack.TwoLayersZ2 21.675
Structure.InterlayerDistance 3.35
Structure.CellHeight 40.0

Intralayer.F2G2Model .true.
TB.NeighLevels 5
TB.Hopping 3.5
TB.OnSiteC 0.4914
Interlayer.TypeOfBL Koshino
Interlayer.KoshinoSR .true.
Interlayer.RenormalizeCoupling .true.
Interlayer.CouplingFactor 1.008     # rigid lattice; 0.895 is the value used with relaxed structures

Kubo.Calc .false.
Diag.Calc .true.
Calculate.Spectral .true.
Spectral.WeiKu .true.              # unfolded weight per layer and sublattice, one file for each
MagField.Integer 0

Spectral.NumPoints 20              # points on the first leg; the others in proportion to their length
&begin Spectral.Path 4
0.67032967 0.27472527 0.0   # K1 - (K2 - K1)
0.66666667 0.33333333 0.0   # K1: Dirac point of the layer(s) aligned with the reference lattice
0.66300366 0.39194139 0.0   # K2: Dirac point of the rotated layer
0.65934066 0.45054945 0.0   # K2 + (K2 - K1)
&end Spectral.Path

# Spectral.Emin and Spectral.Emax are in eV. The energy column of the output files is in units
# of TB.Hopping (3.5 eV here): plot.py multiplies it back to eV.
# Spectral.energyGridResolution is in eV: a state adds its weight to every energy point closer
# than this. The run prints a warning if the points are more than twice that apart, because
# states would then fall between them and be missing from the output.
Spectral.GaussianConvolution .false.
Kubo.NumberofEnergyPoints 301
Spectral.Emin 0.0-1.0
Spectral.Emax 1.2
Spectral.energyGridResolution 0.005

Neigh.fastNNnotsquare .true.
Neigh.LayerNeighbors 400
Neigh.LayerDistFactor 4.0
Output.WriteDataFiles .false.
